            <ArticleTitle>Headaches, rapidly progressive visual loss, and bilateral disc edema.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E133-4; discussion E141-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The diagnosis and management of a 28-year-old obese woman who presented with neck pain, headache, and rapidly progressive visual loss is discussed here. Results of her initial general examination were normal. Thorough medical follow-up resulted in a rare diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
